<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Papua Act 1905</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1905">1905</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Papua Act 1905 was a law of the Australian Parliament that accepted British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and made it the Territory of Papua, administered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>. It came into force in 1906, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-moresby">Port Moresby</a> as capital, and governed the territory until it was joined administratively with the Territory of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p></div>
